  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We create more than a hundred new videos every year. They are the culmination of hundreds of hours of researching, writing, animating, editing, and producing. We comb through thousands of scientific papers from the peer-reviewed medical literature so that busy people like you don’t have to. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In 2022, I covered topics from athletics and atrial fibrillation to vitamin supplements and wrinkles. Which videos floated to the top of the charts this year? Check out the top ten.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#10 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Purported Benefits of Vitamin K2: Should You Take Supplements?</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-90246\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Vitamin capsules on dark background\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>This video just came out and has already become one of the most popular of the year. To summarize, there is no good evidence that vitamin K has bone, brain, or heart benefits beyond its blood-clotting function. And, even if such evidence arose, we can get all of the vitamin K we need from eating greens, since there’s no requirement specifically for vitamin K2. Further, if some evidence did arise that there was some unique benefit from K2, our microbiome makes K2 from the K1 we get from greens. And, even if we had a problem with our microbiome, we can make K1 from K2, just like other animals do. So, the bottom line: Eat your greens.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#9 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to Treat <i>H. Pylori</i> Naturally with Diet</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88004\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"fresh broccoli sprouts in a spoon over cloth\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/58-23-how-to-treat-h-pylori-naturally-with-diet.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>This video asks and answers the question: </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What</span></i><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> food can eradicate </span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">H. pylori</span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in the majority of patients?</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> For some background on the Achilles’ heel in certain Asian diets, check out </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-role-of-kimchi-and-h-pylori-in-stomach-cancer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Role of Kimchi and </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">H. Pylori</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in Stomach Cancer</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#8 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-for-hair-growth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Food for Hair Growth</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-for-hair-growth/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-86240\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"roasted pumpkin seeds on cloth over black surface\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>This video captured the eighth spot in our top ten, but I also covered </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/supplements-for-hair-growth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Supplements for Hair Growth</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/pills-for-hair-growth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pills for Hair Growth</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in case you want to take an even deeper dive. Note I added a correction to the pepper information in the table around minute 2:40. As our new in-house video fact-checker just pointed out, the mg/g values for capsaicin weren’t for regular fresh peppers, but fresh peppers that were then dried! So, it’s a little more daunting. Instead of “a quarter of a fresh jalapeño,” it’s more like “a third of a habanero or a teaspoon of medium-hot red pepper spice.”</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#7 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vitamin-c-supplements-help-with-anxiety/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Do Vitamin C Supplements Help with Anxiety?</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vitamin-c-supplements-help-with-anxiety/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71424\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Yellow supplement pills\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-25.-Do-Vitamin-C-Supplements-Help-with-Anxiety.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>A few months ago, the acclaimed U.S. Preventive Services Task Force published a recommendation to begin screening kids for anxiety starting at age eight. I’m planning to create an entire series of videos next year on dealing with anxiety, but until then, check out this video discussing the risks and benefits of using vitamin C for depression and anxiety.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#6 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/glycemic-index-of-potatoes-why-you-should-chill-and-reheat-them/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Glycemic Index of Potatoes: Why You Should Chill and Reheat Them</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/glycemic-index-of-potatoes-why-you-should-chill-and-reheat-them/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71400\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"cooked potatoes in a pot\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-22-Why-You-Should-Chill-Then-Reheat-Your-Potatoes.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>If you eat potatoes when they’re cold, as in potato salad, or chilled and reheated, you can get a nearly 40 percent lower glycemic impact. Chilling isn’t the only trick to blunting glycemic impact. You can also add vinegar, lemon, or broccoli. See </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-reduce-the-glycemic-impact-of-potatoes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Reduce the Glycemic Impact of Potatoes</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for more information, and, if you’re in a particularly spuddy mood, check out these others from last year: </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-potatoes-increase-the-risk-of-diabetes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do Potatoes Increase the Risk of Diabetes?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-potatoes-increase-the-risk-of-high-blood-pressure-and-death/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do Potatoes Increase the Risk of High Blood Pressure and Death?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-healthiest-type-of-potato/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Healthiest Type of Potato</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#5 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-heal-a-leaky-gut-with-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to Heal a Leaky Gut with Diet</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-heal-a-leaky-gut-with-diet/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70128\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"High fiber super foods with whole grain crackers, fruit, vegetables, whole wheat pasta, grains, and nuts\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>In this video, which took fifth place in our top ten, I address the foods and food components that can boost the integrity of our intestinal barrier. If you missed the backgrounder video, check out </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/avoid-these-foods-to-prevent-a-leaky-gut/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Avoid These Foods to Prevent a Leaky Gut</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, in which I talk about the over-the-counter drugs and diets that make things worse.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#4 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-foods-are-anti-inflammatory/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Which Foods Are Anti-Inflammatory?</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-foods-are-anti-inflammatory/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70739\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"spice and herb collection in bowls and spoons on a black wooden background\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-17.-Which-Foods-Are-Anti-Inflammatory.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>A whole food, plant-based diet is basically synonymous with an anti-inflammatory diet, whereas i</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">nflammatory markers can double within six hours of eating a pro-inflammatory meal, which I cover in the companion video </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/foods-that-cause-inflammation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Foods That Cause Inflammation</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. This may help explain the remarkable findings in another popular video this year: </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/plant-based-eating-score-put-to-the-test/?queryID=e4a95988d4611d2fef9462e0330a53ab/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plant-Based Eating Score Put to the Test</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. So, </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-dont-people-eat-healthier/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Don’t People Eat Healthier?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> That’s another one of my favorites released in 2022!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#3 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Best Diet for Treating Atrial Fibrillation</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88133\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Blue illustration of circulatory system\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-02-the-best-diet-for-treating-atrial-fibrillation.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>This important video is a long time coming, addressing which foods we should eat and avoid to reduce our risk of Afib. It’s chock full of information and ends with a compelling and emotional case report of the power of evidence-based nutrition to reverse disease.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#2 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/fighting-the-ten-hallmarks-of-cancer-with-food/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fighting the Ten Hallmarks of Cancer with Food</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/fighting-the-ten-hallmarks-of-cancer-with-food/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70337\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Plant foods high in fiber with whole wheat pasta, nuts, fruit and vegetables on a rustic background\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>As you may know, I’ve been researching and writing a new book on longevity. After it’s been put to bed, edited, fact-checked, copyedited, and published, and I’ve completed my book tour, my next book will be on cancer survival; so, there will be a lot more forthcoming on this critically important topic. Until then, I have dozens of videos on cancer prevention and treatment, including a mind-blowing series on chemotherapy released this year that asked and answered the questions: </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-effective-is-chemotherapy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Effective Is Chemotherapy?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-much-does-chemotherapy-improve-survival/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Much Does Chemotherapy Improve Survival?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><strong>#1 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Best Diet for Healthy Aging</a></strong></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88147\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Assortment of vegetables, dried beans, and berries\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px\"/></a>2023 is the year my new book </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Age</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> will be released. It’s heartening that there is so much interest, as evidenced by this video reaching number one, as well as the popularity of two other 2022 hits—</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-boost-fgf21-with-diet-for-longevity/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Boost FGF21 with Diet for Longevity</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-increase-your-life-expectancy-12-to-14-years/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Increase Your Life Expectancy 12 to 14 Years</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. And these just scratch the surface. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I can’t wait to share everything else I’ve uncovered!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>"
